1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * He married for the first time in 1711 to the seventeen-year-old Lydia de Hautefort Marquise de Surville (1694–1715). She was the daughter of Marshal Louis Charles d'Hautefort . He had met her in 1710 during the s
2 CONC iege of Douai; she died young and childless after four years of marriage.
2 CONT * The second, also childless marriage was entered into on June 9, 1718 with Anna Margaretha, Baroness Thurn-Valsassina (* October 22, 1694; † May 2, 1730). During the count's absence, her brother Josef Leodegar Thurn, the chief ba
2 CONC iliff of Rosenberg, took over the administration of the count's estates.
2 CONT * In 1733, he married for the third time, to Francisca Romana de la Rochee (died August 20, 1752). This marriage produced two daughters: Karoline and Franziska. Since both daughters were still minors when their father died, Franz 
2 CONC Rodeni Baron von Hirzenau, the Imperial and Royal Provincial Councillor of Moravia, was appointed as their guardian.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_Rudolph_von_Hohenems
