1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigismond_Thalberg
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigismond Thalberg[1] (January 8, 1812 – April 27, 1871) was a composer and one of the most distinguished virtuoso pianists of the 19th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Descent and family background
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigismond Thalberg was born in Pâquis near Geneva, Switzerland, on January 8, 1812. According to his birth certificate, he was the son of "Joseph Thalberg" and "Fortunée Stein", both from Frankfurt-am-Main, but the names in the bi
2 CONC rth certificate are now regarded as fictitious.
2 CONT
2 CONT The identity of Thalberg's mother is now generally accepted as Baroness Maria Julia Wetzlar von Plankenstern. She was born Julia Bydeskuty von Ipp, from a Hungarian family of a lower rank of the nobility. In 1820 she married Baron
2 CONC  Alexander Ludwig Wetzlar von Plankenstern.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thalberg's father is believed to have been Prince Franz Joseph von Dietrichstein who also held the title 'von Thalberg'. Prince von Dietrichstein was unable to marry Thalberg's mother as he was already married (to Alexandrine Coun
2 CONC tess Schuwalow in 1797).
