1 NAME Ferdinand Graf von Harrach zu Rohrau und Thannhausen
1 NAME Ferdinand Friedrich Wilhelm /Graf von Harrach/
2 GIVN Ferdinand Friedrich Wilhelm
2 SURN Graf von Harrach
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 FEB 1832
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rozkochów
3 STAE Opole Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1915
2 ADDR
3 CITY Berlin
3 STAE Berlin
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Rittergutsbesitzer, Maler, Graf von Harrach, Herr auf Rosnochau u. Gross-Sägwitz, Geheimer Rat des Deutschen Kaisers
1 TITL Graf
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.deutsche-biographie.de/sfz26939.htm http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00183742&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Ferdinand, Graf von Harrach zu Rohrau und Thannhausen, was born on 27 February 1832 in Rosnochau, the son of Karl Philip, Graf von Harrach zu Rohrau und Thannhausen, and Theresia, Gräfin Sedlnitzky von Choltic. His godmo
2 CONC ther was his aunt Auguste, the morganatic wife of Friedrich Wilhelm III, King of Prussia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand was educated privately on his father's estate in Schnepfenthal. In 1847 he attended the Maria Magdalenen Gymnasium in Breslau. A journey with his parents to Italy, including a long stay in Rome, encouraged Ferdinand to p
2 CONC ursue his artistic ambitions. 
2 CONT
2 CONT However his father wanted him to succed him as the owner of the family's estate and sent him to Berlin to study, but he painted and drew in his spare time. In 1856 and 1857 he completed his military service with the Cuirassiers in
2 CONC  Breslau. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His father requested an examination of his son's artistic work by Stanislaus, Graf von Kalckreuth, Professor of the Düsseldorf Art Academy, whose opinion was favourable and Ferdinand was finally allowed to study art. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand undertook several trips, mostly in the Alpine areas, but also to the British Isles. In the war of 1866 he served as a Prussian officer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 26 August 1868 in Oberhofen bei Thun he married Hélène, Gräfin von Pourtales, daughter of Albert Alexandre, Graf von Pourtales, and Anna von Bethmann-Hollweg. They became the parents of eight children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of his paintings were displayed in exhibitions in Berlin and Dresden, and he began to receive commissions from the nobility to paint their portraits. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1871 he participated with the designs for the new German coat of arms for the coronation of Emperor Wilhelm I. In 1873 he received an inheritance from his aunt Auguste which enabled him to buy a castle which, after renovations,
2 CONC  became the family home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1892 Ferdinand was appointed Professor and in 1893 as Senator of the Royal Academy of Arts. In 1899, with his wife, he travelled to Egypt, and his works displayed a biblical theme. Ferdinand was one of the last representatives 
2 CONC of classical painting. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand died on 14 February 1915 in Berlin. His widow died on 13 December 1940 in Kraschnitz.
