3 STAE Mähren
3 CTRY Czech Republic
1 OCCU Regierender Fürst von Liechtenstein
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Golden Fleece - Austian Branch===
2 CONT *[http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~prohel/names/misc/liechtenstein.html#franz1 '''rootsweg.ancestry.com...''']
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_I,_Prince_of_Liechtenstein '''Wikipedia....''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Franz I, Prince of Liechtenstein''', born '''Franz de Paula Maria Karl August''' ([http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schloss_Liechtenstein Schloss Liechtenstein], 28 August 1853 – [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feldsberg Feldsberg], 
2 CONC 25 July 1938) was the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liechtenstein Prince of Liechtenstein] between 1929 and 1938. He was the son of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloys_II_of_Liechtenstein '''Aloys II of Liechtenstein'''] and his w
2 CONC ife [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franziska_Kinsky_of_Wchinitz_and_Tettau '''Countess Franziska Kinsky''']. '''Franz''' succeeded his older brother [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_II,_Prince_of_Liechtenstein '''Johann II'''],
2 CONC  as Prince of Liechtenstein in 1929.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Franz I''' served as the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austria-Hungary Austro-Hungarian] ambassador at the Court of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicholas_II_of_Russia Tsar Nicholas II] in [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Pete
2 CONC rsburg St. Petersburg] between 1894 and 1899. As Prince of Liechtenstein, he continued the economic reforms initiated by his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like his brother '''Johann II''',''' Franz I''' had no children. His first cousin once removed [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Aloys_of_Liechtenstein '''Prince Aloys'''] was [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heir_presumptive heir
2 CONC  presumptive], but '''Aloys''' removed himself from the line of succession in favor of his son, [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_Joseph_II,_Prince_of_Liechtenstein '''Franz Josef'''], in 1921.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Franz I''' married hereditary Baroness [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elisabeth_von_Gutmann '''Elisabeth von Gutmann'''] ([http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vienna Vienna], 8 January 1875 - [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitznau Vitzn
2 CONC au], 28 September 1947), a noblewoman of Jewish descent, on 22 July 1929 in Vienna, without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the 1,204th [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight Knight] of the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Order_of_the_Golden_Fleece Order of the Golden Fleece] in Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT In March 1938 the elderly '''Franz I''' named '''Franz Joseph''' the country's [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regent regent]. Although he cited old age as his reason for relinquishing his duties, it is widely believed that it was b
2 CONC ecause he had no desire to be on the throne if [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nazi_Germany Nazi Germany] invaded his small [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality Principality]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Franz I''' died on 25 July 1938, and was formally succeeded by '''Franz Joseph''', who became [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_Joseph_II,_Prince_of_Liechtenstein '''Franz Joseph II, Prince of Liechtenstein'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Franz-Joseph I, Prince de LIECHTENSTEIN - Fils de Emanuel von und zu LIECHTENSTEIN (1700-1771) et de Comtesse Maria Antonia von DIETRICHSTEIN - né Milan 1726 - + Metz 1781 - ep. 1750 Comtesse Maria Leopoldine von STERNBERG (1733-1
2 CONC 809) - 8 enfants dont: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.	Princesse Leopoldine Adelgunde von und zu LIECHTENSTEIN - née 1754 - + 1823 - ep. 1771 Landgrave Karl Emanuel de HESSE-RHEINFELS-ROTENBURG (+ 1812) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.	Princesse Maria Antonia von und zu LIECHTENSTEIN - Religieuse à Essen - née 1756 - + 1821 
2 CONT
