1 NOTE He was the last Bourbon ruler of the Two Sicilies. He tried to continue 
2 CONT the autocratic policies of his father, but his kingdom was lost in the 
2 CONT unification of Italy. In 1860 the kingdom was invaded by revolutionary 
2 CONT troops under the Italian nationalist leader Giuseppe Garibaldi, and it was 
2 CONT forced to capitulate the following year. Compelled to abdicate in 1861, 
2 CONT Francis lived thereafter in various European countries, from which he 
2 CONT occasionally organized abortive conspiracies against the new kingdom of 
2 CONT Italy.
