2 CONT From: Maureen and Paul Baltay <msbpmb@erols.com>
2 CONT Entry from the Pallas lexicon.  A loose, not a literal translation is:
2 CONT
2 CONT Odescalchi (pronounced odeszkálki) is a family of Italian origin with a Hungarian branch.  One member, Benedict O., served as Pope Innocent XI. His nephew, Livius, was elevated to a prince of the empire by Emperor Leopold I, who g
2 CONC ave him the Szerémség [term for several counties, Szerém, Veröcze etc. south of the Drava River] with the title in 1698. After the death of Livius in 1713, the title passed to the Erba-Odescalchi family from Milan.  Livius II (172
2 CONC 5-1800) is from this branch of the family and he was indigenated [a formal step in which a family's nobility is recognized as Hungarian nobility] in 1751. Hungarian members of the O. family are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Prince Arthur O., member of the K und K cabinet, born in Szalcsány, Nyitra County [now Slovakia] on July 21,1837.  He studied at Pozsony [now Bratislava] and Lipcse, and spent several years in Switzerland and Rome.  After he c
2 CONC ame home, he became a Captain in the Hungarian army and commander of the Nyitra regiment.  He represented Tapolca (1881) and Vág-Vecse (1886) in Parliament on a platform of independence.  Currently (1896) he is a member of the upp
2 CONC er house.  On June 5, 1873, he became a director of the Hungarian historical society.  He is also a director of the Hungarian archaelogical and genealogical societies.  His book about Hungarian history, "Memories out of the Past o
2 CONC f Bars County" was published in Budapest in 1892 under the pseudonym of Szerémi.  He has written numerous articles in various journals.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur, prince, royal and imperial chamberlain, was born in Szalcsany (Nyitra county) 1837, jul. 21.  He studied in Pozsony and completed his studies at the university of Lipcse.  He spent quite some time in Switzerland and Roma, 
2 CONC also.  He joined the Hungarian national guard and became commander of the Nyitra battalion.  He was elected representative  for the Tapolca district in 1881 and for the Vag-Vecsei district in 1886.  Currently, (1896) he is a membe
2 CONC r of the upper house of Parliament.  He was elected in a leadership role as a member of the historical society, and as the same of the national archeological and the genealogical societies.  He has written Hungarian historical wor
2 CONC ks under the name of Szeremi.  "Memories of Bars County's History" (Budapest 1892).  He has several articles published in journals such as Szazadok and Tortenelmi Tar.«s44»
